		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://nursesrevisionuganda.com/?p=3972#comment-355</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[In reply to &lt;a href=&quot;https://nursesrevisionuganda.com/acute-pericarditis/#comment-350&quot;&gt;Inno&lt;/a&gt;.

Is reduced body activity an allowed Nursing Diagnosis?, No, Check Nanda for more clarity]]></description>
			<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>In reply to <a href="https://nursesrevisionuganda.com/acute-pericarditis/#comment-350">Inno</a>.</p>
<p>Is reduced body activity an allowed Nursing Diagnosis?, No, Check Nanda for more clarity</p>
]]></content:encoded>
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>
		By: Inno		</title>
		<link>https://nursesrevisionuganda.com/acute-pericarditis/#comment-350</link>

		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Inno]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 12 Jul 2023 07:17:47 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://nursesrevisionuganda.com/?p=3972#comment-350</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[Is it reduced cardiac output related to pericarditis as evidenced by fatigue and in ability to do activities of daily living as normal.
Or it should have been reduced body activity related to pericarditis evidenced by fatigue and inability to do daily living activities as normal??
In that&#039; part of nursing diagnosis <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f64f.png" alt="🙏" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" />]]></description>
			<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Is it reduced cardiac output related to pericarditis as evidenced by fatigue and in ability to do activities of daily living as normal.<br />
Or it should have been reduced body activity related to pericarditis evidenced by fatigue and inability to do daily living activities as normal??<br />
In that&#8217; part of nursing diagnosis 🙏</p>
]]></content:encoded>
		
			</item>
